},[107,548,550],{"href":549},"\u002Flinux\u002F19-exercises-and-projects","Exercises & Projects",[101,552,553],{},"8 projects from a hardened web server to a capstone cluster.",[19,555,557],{"id":556},"learning-path-suggestions","Learning Path Suggestions",[72,559,561],{"id":560},"if-youre-a-developer-deploying-to-linux","If you're a developer deploying to Linux",[15,563,564],{},"Read 08 (package management), 10 (networking — ports, firewall), 11 (systemd — running your app as a service), 14 (security — UFW, SSH keys), 17 (containers). Do exercise 4 (hardened web server).",[72,566,568],{"id":567},"if-youre-an-aspiring-sysadmin","If you're an aspiring sysadmin",[15,570,571],{},"Read 09 (storage, LVM), 11 (systemd), 12 (logging), 13 (kernel), 15 (performance), 16 (boot), 18 (troubleshooting). Do exercises 5–7 (monitoring, backup, cluster). Bookmark 18 — you'll need it at 3 AM.",[72,573,575],{"id":574},"if-youre-preparing-for-lpicrhcsa","If you're preparing for LPIC\u002FRHCSA",[15,577,578],{},"Read 03–12 (filesystem, permissions, processes, users, packages, storage, networking, systemd, logging). Then 13–16 (kernel, security, performance, boot). Do all exercises in 19.",[19,580,582],{"id":581},"companion-resources","Companion Resources",[56,584,585,594,602,610,618],{},[27,586,587,593],{},[107,588,592],{"href":589,"rel":590},"https:\u002F\u002Fwiki.archlinux.org",[591],"nofollow","Arch Wiki"," — the best Linux reference, distro-agnostic.",[27,595,596,601],{},[107,597,600],{"href":598,"rel":599},"https:\u002F\u002Fman7.org\u002Flinux\u002Fman-pages\u002F",[591],"Linux man pages online"," — authoritative man pages.",[27,603,604,609],{},[107,605,608],{"href":606,"rel":607},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.freedesktop.org\u002Fwiki\u002FSoftware\u002Fsystemd\u002F",[591],"systemd documentation"," — the init system reference.",[27,611,612,617],{},[107,613,616],{"href":614,"rel":615},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.kernel.org",[591],"Linux Kernel Archives"," — kernel source, docs.",[27,619,620